We started with the original code which was very slow.
We then implemented partDist using matrix calculations instead of recursion. The matrix calculations was the most significant speedup
We then stopped or skipped the calculations if the distance could not be shorter than the current best. This had a speedup of around 5x.
We realized that this was not going to work because it took us around 8 seconds to go through 500k words with 100 queries.
We then grouped each word by length in order to be able to not have to go thorugh the whole list of words.
This created a speedup of around 8x which was enough to pass all kattis test (last test was 1.01 s)